<div id="nozzlealign_tab">
  <div class="row-fluid">
    <div class="span7">
      <div class="nozzlealign-view">
        <img data-bind="attr: {src: overlayUrl}" class="nozzlealign-frame">
      </div>
      <p class="muted">
        The blue crosshair is the target. The red circle is the detected tip.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: refreshPreview">Refresh</button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: toggleLive,
                css: {'btn-primary': live}">Live</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="span5">
      <h4>Step 1: find the camera</h4>
      <p class="muted">
        This homes the machine, then moves the toolhead until the camera can see
        the nozzle move. It works out where the camera is and how high to sit
        above it. You do not enter any coordinates.
      </p>
      <p data-bind="text: cameraText, visible: cameraText" class="text-success"></p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: discover,
                enable: !running()">Find the camera</button>
      </div>

      <h4>Step 2: measure the offset</h4>
      <p data-bind="text: cameraWarning, visible: cameraWarning"
         class="text-error"></p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" data-bind="click: run,
                enable: !running() &amp;&amp; !cameraWarning()">Measure offset</button>
        <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: abort,
                enable: running">Stop</button>
      </div>

      <h5>Progress</h5>
      <pre class="nozzlealign-log" data-bind="text: log"></pre>

      <!-- ko if: result -->
      <h5>Result</h5>
      <table class="table table-condensed">
        <tr><th>Stored T1 offset</th>
            <td data-bind="text: storedOffsetText"></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Nozzle 1 needed</th>
            <td data-bind="text: correctionText"></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Residual after centring</th>
            <td data-bind="text: residualText"></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Image scale</th>
            <td data-bind="text: scaleText"></td></tr>
      </table>

      <p>
        The sign of a Marlin hotend offset is not documented for this toolhead,
        so both candidates are shown. Write one, then measure again. The
        correction must fall towards zero. If it doubles, write the other one.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: applyPlus, text: plusLabel"></button>
        <button class="btn" data-bind="click: applyMinus, text: minusLabel"></button>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">
        Prefer the slicer instead? Put the numbers above into the tool offset
        there and write nothing to the firmware.
      </p>
      <!-- /ko -->
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
